# Issue #103: a whole tool-call block naming a tool the request did not offer stays text, as before (it is never made a
# call and never run; names are matched exactly, no namespace is stripped), and is now reported. parse_tool_calls takes
# a `rejected` list and gets the generated name of each block that parsed as a call (GLM, Qwen or JSON markup) to an
# unoffered tool; the server's end parser collects them per reply. TF_GLM_TOOL_DIAGNOSTICS: unset (the default) logs
# one line, `[tensorfold] tool call rejected: unknown_tool_name ['exec'] (1 tools offered); kept as text`: the generated
# names only, never an argument value or the prompt; 1 also lists them in the reply's `tensorfold` block (the last
# event of a stream) as `tool_call_rejections: [{"reason": "unknown_tool_name", "name": "exec"}]`, so a gateway can
# tell the reply from an ordinary answer and re-prompt; 0 does neither. Generated tokens, the reply's text, its calls
# and its finish_reason are unchanged in every mode. tools/tool_diagnostics_check.py.

